    "body": "fix on issue/1659-face-tangent-gouge · PR #1668 · pinned by face_stock_edge::a_face_row_tangent_to_the_stock_edge_in_air_with_no_part_is_clean_and_posts, face_stock_edge::the_same_face_over_a_part_whose_top_stands_above_cut_z_is_refused, face_stock_edge::a_tangent_last_row_0_02_mm_into_a_part_is_refused, boundary_walls::a_row_through_two_side_vertices_tangent_to_the_far_edge_crosses_the_rim_and_is_clean, boundary_walls::a_move_inside_or_only_touching_a_vertex_still_answers_to_the_walls · merges when reviewed\n\nRoot cause: the stock outline has vertices on its straight sides, at (-2, 60) and (62, 60). The last row goes exactly through them. Thus it crosses no edge interior, and the Boundary wall reading with no model (`wall_gouge` in `crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs`) read it as a move in the region, at distance 0 from a vertex. The fix counts a pass through a vertex with its neighbours on opposite sides as a rim crossing. No tolerance changed.\n",
